{0 ocsipersist-sqlite}

SQLite backend for Ocsipersist.
For the API documentation see OPAM package {{:../ocsipersist/Ocsipersist/index.html}ocsipersist}.
This page describes how to configure the SQLite backend.

{1 Using as a library}

If you are not using Ocsigen Server's configuration file,
add library [ocsipersist-sqlite.settings] in your Dune file, and
use module {!Ocsipersist_settings} to configure the storage file.
The database file is required: there is no default. The directory of the
file must exist. Set it before calling [Ocsipersist.init ()] and before
the first access to the database, otherwise they fail with an error asking
for it.

Creating a persistent reference, a [Store_json] value or a table does not
access the database: it is accessed at the first [get], [set], [find] or
other use of the value. So these values can be created before the file is
set, for instance when a module is initialised. [Store.open_store] and
[Store.make_persistent] access the database when called. An access that
fails because the file is not set yet does not break the value: the next
access tries again. Each access uses the file set when it is made.

{[
let () =
  Ocsipersist_settings.set_db_file "data/ocsidb";
  Ocsipersist.init ()
]}


{1 Using with Ocsigen Server: ocsipersist-sqlite-config}

If you want to configure Ocsipersist-sqlite from Ocsigen Server's
configuration file, use package
{{:../ocsipersist-sqlite-config/Ocsipersist_config/index.html}ocsipersist-sqlite-config}.
